### Poll & Survey Builder - manual API tests
###
### Run all four projects first (PollManage, VoteManage, ResultManage, ApiGateway),
### then click "Send request" above each block below.
###
### Everything here goes through the GATEWAY on port 5000, which is what the Vue app
### uses too. Testing against the gateway means you are testing the real path.
###
### After step 1, copy the "code" and "creatorToken" out of the response into the
### two variables just below.

@gateway = http://localhost:5000

# Paste from the response of step 1:
@code = PASTE_CODE_HERE
@creatorToken = PASTE_CREATOR_TOKEN_HERE


### 1. Create a poll -> 201 Created
### Copy "code" and "creatorToken" from the response into the variables above.
POST {{gateway}}/api/polls
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Tabs or spaces?",
  "options": ["Tabs", "Spaces", "I do not care"]
}


### 2. Read the poll back -> 200 OK
GET {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}


### 3. Vote as browser A -> 200 OK
### The X-Voter-Token is how the server tells browsers apart. Any text works for testing.
POST {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json
X-Voter-Token: browser-a

{
  "optionIndex": 0
}


### 4. Vote AGAIN as browser A -> 409 Conflict
### This is the one-vote-per-person rule. Send it twice, it stays 409.
POST {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json
X-Voter-Token: browser-a

{
  "optionIndex": 1
}


### 5. Vote as browser B -> 200 OK
### A different token means a different person, so this one is allowed.
POST {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json
X-Voter-Token: browser-b

{
  "optionIndex": 1
}


### 6. Vote for an option that does not exist -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json
X-Voter-Token: browser-c

{
  "optionIndex": 5
}


### 7. Live results -> 200 OK
### This comes from ResultManage, which asked PollManage for the option text and
### VoteManage for the counts, then joined them.
GET {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/results


### 8. The raw counts VoteManage owns -> 200 OK
### Just numbers, no option text, because VoteManage does not have the Polls table.
### Useful for showing what each service actually owns.
GET {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/vote/counts


### 9. Has this browser voted already? -> 200 OK
GET {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/vote/me
X-Voter-Token: browser-a


### 10. Download the results as CSV -> 200 OK
GET {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/results.csv


### 11. Try to edit after people have voted -> 409 Conflict
### The question is frozen once the first vote lands.
PATCH {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Creator-Token: {{creatorToken}}

{
  "question": "A completely different question?"
}


### 12. Try to close WITHOUT the creator token -> 403 Forbidden
POST {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/close


### 13. Close the poll properly -> 200 OK
POST {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/close
X-Creator-Token: {{creatorToken}}


### 14. Vote after closing -> 409 Conflict
POST {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}/vote
Content-Type: application/json
X-Voter-Token: browser-d

{
  "optionIndex": 0
}


### 15. Reopen the poll -> 200 OK
### PATCH changes only what you send, so this only touches the status.
PATCH {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Creator-Token: {{creatorToken}}

{
  "status": "Open"
}


### 16. A poll code that does not exist -> 404 Not Found
GET {{gateway}}/api/polls/zzzzzz


### 17. Replace the whole poll with PUT -> 200 OK, or 409 if it has votes
### PUT needs every field, unlike PATCH.
PUT {{gateway}}/api/polls/{{code}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Creator-Token: {{creatorToken}}

{
  "question": "Which editor?",
  "options": ["Visual Studio", "VS Code"]
}
